hind the distinction between "the pump" and "the heart." You forced me to see that. But the spirit of your original question was about whether using your heart hard—exercising—wears it out the way using a hip does. And on that, the answer remains no. The part that does the hard work gets stronger. The parts that wear are on their own timeline, often unrelated to fitness, and even they fare better in a body that moves. I'm not relabeling. I'm acknowledging that the heart is a system, not a monolith. Some parts of that system are fragile timers. Some are self-renewing muscle. The muscle—the part you were worried about—is the closest thing we have to a biological perpetual motion machine, and it thrives on the very load you feared would break it.
